{% comment %}
  FUEL_04 cart drawer ladder. Rendered from snippets/cart-drawer.liquid,
  inside .drawer__inner and above the line items.

  Why there and not in a script: cart-drawer.js re-renders .drawer__inner (and
  #CartDrawer on add) through the section rendering API on every cart change,
  so a bar that lives inside that element is redrawn by Liquid with the fresh
  cart on every add, remove and quantity change. That is why the bar needs no
  JavaScript: the gift script in snippets/fuel04-global.liquid writes the cart
  and never draws here.

  Shape from frames 127:150993 and 127:151012: a rail with a #003900 fill and
  round chips standing on it, a caption under the chips that carry a reward,
  then a #f1f2ee strip with an icon and one sentence, in that order.

  Content from the brief, not from those frames. The frames still draw the free
  shipping and 10 / 15 / 20 % ladder this test replaces; the brief sets the
  ladder to 1 | 2 | 3 gift 30 ml GRATIS | 4 | 5 gift +100 ml MYSTERY. Every
  chip and caption is a theme setting, so a ruling the other way needs no
  deploy.

  Display only. It states the offer, it does not grant it: the free 30 ml and
  the mystery 100 ml come from the gift app's (Kite) two offers, whose codes
  snippets/fuel04-global.liquid puts on the cart. Nothing here writes a line
  item property, a discount code or a cart attribute.

  The app owned gift ladder that is already in this drawer (Kite) is hidden for
  the variant only, at the end of assets/fuel04-multibuy.css. Hidden, not
  removed: the app keeps running and keeps adding its own gift.

  Every number and every string is a theme setting, under "FUEL_04 Multi-buy"
  in theme settings. This snippet has no section of its own to hang settings on
  because layout/theme.liquid renders the drawer as a snippet, not a section.
  Write [n] in a line where the number of bottles still needed should appear,
  and put the part that should stand out in green between asterisks.

  Swedish market only, like the rest of the test. The gate below cannot tell
  the markets apart on its own (one Shopify locale, Weglot at the edge), so
  what actually keeps this off the Danish, Finnish and Norwegian pages is the
  market guard in snippets/fuel04-global.liquid and its belt in
  assets/fuel04-multibuy.css.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign fuel04_tier_1 = settings.fuel04_cart_tier_1
  assign fuel04_tier_2 = settings.fuel04_cart_tier_2
  assign fuel04_size = settings.fuel04_cart_size_token | downcase | strip | replace: ' ', ''
  assign fuel04_gift_id = settings.fuel04_gift_variant_tier_2 | strip
-%}
{%- if request.locale.iso_code == 'sv' and cart != empty and fuel04_tier_2 > 0 and fuel04_tier_1 > 0 -%}
  {%- liquid
    comment
      What counts is a single bottle of the size the offer is written for, the
      same unit the gift app (Kite) counts when it grants the gift: the variant
      title compared with the token WHOLE, on the normalised strings (downcased,
      spaces out). A substring test once read "Doftar som... Si Passione - No.
      100" as eligible when its 30 ml was bought three times.

      Multi bottle boxes ("5X 100ml") and bottles sold without a size variant
      used to count from their product name. They no longer do: Kite counts
      only the single 100 ml bottles of the test perfumes, so a box lit both
      gifts here while checkout gave neither. Whether a box should count is the
      strategist's call; if it should, the gift app's offer has to change first.

      Gift lines never count: the mystery bottle snippets/fuel04-global.liquid
      puts in itself (the variant in theme settings), and every line the gift app adds
      (property _free_product, a FREEGIFT discount). The app auto-adds "Gömd
      Skatt" and "Gratis Mystik Parfym", and the price cannot be the test,
      because the same app once ran the shop's 2+1 deal, which made the
      shopper's own third bottle cost nothing (QA, Sep 16).

      An empty token counts every line in the cart that is not a gift.
    endcomment
    assign fuel04_count = 0
    for line_item in cart.items
      assign line_vid = line_item.variant_id | append: ''
      if line_vid == fuel04_gift_id or line_item.properties._free_product == 'true'
        continue
      endif
      assign line_is_gift = false
      for allocation in line_item.line_level_discount_allocations
        if allocation.discount_application.title contains 'FREEGIFT'
          assign line_is_gift = true
        endif
      endfor
      if line_is_gift
        continue
      endif

      assign line_variant = line_item.variant.title | downcase | strip | replace: ' ', ''
      if fuel04_size == blank or line_variant == fuel04_size
        assign fuel04_count = fuel04_count | plus: line_item.quantity
      endif
    endfor

    comment
      The rail is the cart frame's own (Figma 211:2623): the numbered steps
      with a reward node after each tier, tier_2 + 2 nodes spread evenly over
      a 373 px rail, and a 5 px track inset 10 px at both ends (347 px). The
      fill ends on the middle of the last lit number, on the near edge of a
      lit reward node (the frame draws 161 of 347 at three bottles), and runs
      the whole track once the last reward is reached. Node pitch is
      (373 - 32.109) / (nodes - 1); everything below is a share of the track,
      so a narrower drawer keeps the same picture.
    endcomment
    assign fuel04_reached = fuel04_count | at_most: fuel04_tier_2
    assign fuel04_nodes = fuel04_tier_2 | plus: 2
    assign fuel04_pct = 0
    if fuel04_reached >= fuel04_tier_2
      assign fuel04_pct = 100
    elsif fuel04_reached > 0
      assign fuel04_gaps = fuel04_nodes | minus: 1
      assign fuel04_pitch = 340.891 | divided_by: fuel04_gaps
      assign fuel04_idx = fuel04_reached | minus: 1
      assign fuel04_offset = 16.054
      if fuel04_reached >= fuel04_tier_1
        assign fuel04_idx = fuel04_idx | plus: 1
        if fuel04_reached == fuel04_tier_1
          assign fuel04_offset = 0
        endif
      endif
      assign fuel04_end = fuel04_idx | times: fuel04_pitch | plus: fuel04_offset | minus: 10.0
      assign fuel04_pct = fuel04_end | times: 100.0 | divided_by: 347.0 | round: 2
    endif

    comment
      One bottle left takes the singular line. "Lägg [n] flaskor till" reads
      "Lägg 1 flaskor till" at the last step, and both counting lines land on
      one with the tiers as they are set (3 and 5), so both have a singular of
      their own. An empty singular setting falls back to the plural line rather
      than to nothing.
    endcomment
    if fuel04_count >= fuel04_tier_2
      assign fuel04_line = settings.fuel04_cart_text_done
      assign fuel04_left = 0
    elsif fuel04_count >= fuel04_tier_1
      assign fuel04_left = fuel04_tier_2 | minus: fuel04_count
      assign fuel04_line = settings.fuel04_cart_text_mid
      if fuel04_left == 1 and settings.fuel04_cart_text_mid_one != blank
        assign fuel04_line = settings.fuel04_cart_text_mid_one
      endif
    else
      assign fuel04_left = fuel04_tier_1 | minus: fuel04_count
      assign fuel04_line = settings.fuel04_cart_text_start
      if fuel04_left == 1 and settings.fuel04_cart_text_start_one != blank
        assign fuel04_line = settings.fuel04_cart_text_start_one
      endif
    endif

    comment
      Two readings of the same line. The visible one carries the number in
      bold and the reward phrase in green; the one on the progress bar is
      plain, because assistive tech reads the label as it stands and used to
      be handed the raw [n] placeholder.
    endcomment
    assign fuel04_left_markup = fuel04_left | prepend: '<strong>' | append: '</strong>'
    assign fuel04_line_plain = fuel04_line | replace: '[n]', fuel04_left | replace: '*', ''
  -%}
  {%- capture fuel04_line_html -%}
    {%- assign fuel04_runs = fuel04_line | escape | replace: '[n]', fuel04_left_markup | split: '*' -%}
    {%- for fuel04_run in fuel04_runs -%}
      {%- assign fuel04_odd = forloop.index0 | modulo: 2 -%}
      {%- if fuel04_odd == 1 -%}
        <b class="fuel04-cart__hl">{{ fuel04_run }}</b>
      {%- else -%}
        {{- fuel04_run -}}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- liquid
    comment
      The frame sets each reward label on two lines, the last word on its
      own: "30 ml" over "GRATIS", "+100 ml" over "MYSTERY".
    endcomment
    assign fuel04_label_1_words = settings.fuel04_cart_label_1 | strip | split: ' '
    assign fuel04_label_2_words = settings.fuel04_cart_label_2 | strip | split: ' '
    assign fuel04_label_1_last = fuel04_label_1_words | last
    assign fuel04_label_2_last = fuel04_label_2_words | last
    assign fuel04_label_1_head = ''
    for fuel04_word in fuel04_label_1_words
      unless forloop.last
        assign fuel04_label_1_head = fuel04_label_1_head | append: fuel04_word | append: ' '
      endunless
    endfor
    assign fuel04_label_2_head = ''
    for fuel04_word in fuel04_label_2_words
      unless forloop.last
        assign fuel04_label_2_head = fuel04_label_2_head | append: fuel04_word | append: ' '
      endunless
    endfor
    assign fuel04_label_1_head = fuel04_label_1_head | strip
    assign fuel04_label_2_head = fuel04_label_2_head | strip
    assign fuel04_rail_label = settings.fuel04_cart_label_1 | append: ' · ' | append: settings.fuel04_cart_label_2 | strip
  -%}
  <div class="fuel04 fuel04-cart" style="display: none;">
    <div class="fuel04-cart__row">
      <div
        class="fuel04-cart__rail"
        role="progressbar"
        aria-valuemin="0"
        aria-valuemax="{{ fuel04_tier_2 }}"
        aria-valuenow="{{ fuel04_reached }}"
        aria-label="{{ fuel04_rail_label | escape }}"
        style="--fuel04-fill: {{ fuel04_pct }}%;">
        <div class="fuel04-cart__track"><div class="fuel04-cart__fill"></div></div>
        {%- for fuel04_step in (1..fuel04_tier_2) -%}
          <span class="fuel04-cart__node{% if fuel04_count >= fuel04_step %} is-on{% endif %}">{{ fuel04_step }}</span>
          {%- if fuel04_step == fuel04_tier_1 or fuel04_step == fuel04_tier_2 -%}
            {%- if fuel04_count >= fuel04_step -%}
              <span class="fuel04-cart__gift is-on" aria-hidden="true"><img src="{{ 'fuel04-cart-gift-on.svg' | asset_url }}" width="40" height="40" alt=""></span>
            {%- else -%}
              <span class="fuel04-cart__gift" aria-hidden="true"><img src="{{ 'fuel04-cart-gift-off.svg' | asset_url }}" width="34" height="33" alt=""></span>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- liquid
      comment
        The first reward node stands after tier_1 numbers, so its share of the
        rail is tier_1 over the number of gaps; the second is the last node.
      endcomment
      assign fuel04_label_gaps = fuel04_nodes | minus: 1
      assign fuel04_label_a = fuel04_tier_1 | times: 1.0 | divided_by: fuel04_label_gaps | round: 4
    -%}
    <div class="fuel04-cart__labels" aria-hidden="true" style="--fuel04-label-a: {{ fuel04_label_a }};">
      {%- if settings.fuel04_cart_label_1 != blank -%}
        <span class="fuel04-cart__label fuel04-cart__label--a">{{ fuel04_label_1_head }}{% if fuel04_label_1_head != blank %}<br>{% endif %}{{ fuel04_label_1_last }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if settings.fuel04_cart_label_2 != blank -%}
        <span class="fuel04-cart__label fuel04-cart__label--b">{{ fuel04_label_2_head }}{% if fuel04_label_2_head != blank %}<br>{% endif %}{{ fuel04_label_2_last }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    {%- comment -%}
      The frame draws no message under the rail (the strip of the earlier
      round was removed from the design). The line survives as an option for
      the strategist and stays off until a setting turns it on.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if settings.fuel04_cart_show_message and fuel04_line != blank -%}
      <p class="fuel04-cart__msg">
        <svg
          class="fuel04-cart__msg-icon"
          width="18"
          height="18"
          viewBox="0 0 20.28 20"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="1"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          aria-hidden="true"
          focusable="false">
          <rect x="1.14" y="6.5" width="18" height="3.5" rx="0.75" />
          <path d="M2.64 10v8.25a.75.75 0 0 0 .75.75h13.5a.75.75 0 0 0 .75-.75V10" />
          <path d="M10.14 6.5V19" />
          <path d="M10.14 6.5S9.1 1 6.4 1a2.2 2.2 0 0 0 0 5.5z" />
          <path d="M10.14 6.5s1.04-5.5 3.74-5.5a2.2 2.2 0 0 1 0 5.5z" />
        </svg>
        <span>{{ fuel04_line_html }}</span>
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
